# Nawy Scraper — Setup & Run Guide

## What this scraper collects

| Field | Notes |
|---|---|
| Developer | Name, ID, URL |
| Project (Compound) | Name, ID, area/location |
| Phase | Name, ID — `NULL` when project has no phases |
| `has_phases` flag | Always set — makes no-phase projects explicit |
| Unit type | Apartment, Villa, Townhouse, Duplex, etc. |
| Bedrooms | Integer |
| Bathrooms | Integer |
| Area | Numeric in sqm |
| Price | Numeric value |
| Currency | `EGP`, `USD`, `EUR`, `AED`, `SAR` — auto-detected |
| Payment plan | Down payment %, instalment years, description |
| Unit URL | Direct link to unit on Nawy |

---

## Prerequisites

- Python 3.11+
- PostgreSQL (local or remote)
- ~2 GB RAM free (Playwright runs Chromium)

---

## Step 1 — Create the database

```bash
createdb nawy_db
psql -U youruser -d nawy_db -f schema.sql
```

---

## Step 2 — Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
playwright install chromium   # downloads ~130MB Chromium binary
```

---

## Step 3 — Configure the connection string

Open `scraper.py` and edit line ~55:

```python
DB_DSN = "postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/nawy_db"
```

---

## Step 4 — Run

```bash
python scraper.py
```

Progress is printed to console AND written to `nawy_scraper.log`.

---

## Expected runtime

| Scale | Approx. time |
|---|---|
| ~100 developers | 5–10 minutes |
| ~800+ compounds | 3–6 hours total |
| 15,000+ units | included in above |

Nawy is polite-scraped at 1.5 sec/page with 3 parallel workers.
Adjust `CONCURRENCY` and `REQUEST_DELAY` in `scraper.py` if needed.

---

## Useful queries after scraping

### All units with currency breakdown
```sql
SELECT currency, COUNT(*), MIN(price), AVG(price)::NUMERIC(18,0), MAX(price)
FROM units
GROUP BY currency
ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC;
```

### Projects without phases
```sql
SELECT * FROM v_projects_no_phases;
```

### Full flat listing
```sql
SELECT * FROM v_full_listing
WHERE developer = 'Mountain View'
ORDER BY phase, price;
```

### Units priced in USD
```sql
SELECT developer, project, phase, unit_type, bedrooms, area_sqm, price
FROM v_full_listing
WHERE currency = 'USD'
ORDER BY price;
```

### Average price per sqm by developer
```sql
SELECT developer_name, currency,
       AVG(price / NULLIF(area_sqm, 0))::NUMERIC(12,0) AS avg_price_per_sqm
FROM units
WHERE area_sqm > 0 AND price > 0
GROUP BY developer_name, currency
ORDER BY avg_price_per_sqm DESC;
```

---

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| `playwright install` fails | Run with `sudo` or check disk space |
| Units not loading | Nawy may have updated their JS — increase `REQUEST_DELAY` to 3 |
| Getting 403 / blocked | Set `CONCURRENCY = 1` and increase delay to 3–4 sec |
| DB connection refused | Check PostgreSQL is running: `pg_isready` |
| `ON CONFLICT` errors | Schema not applied — re-run `schema.sql` |

---

## Architecture diagram

```
/developer (HTML, static)
    └── developer cards → Developer IDs + slugs

/developer/{id}-{slug} (HTML, mostly static)
    └── compound links → Compound IDs + slugs

/compound/{id}-{slug} (JS rendered via Playwright)
    ├── Has "Phases" section?
    │     YES → collect phase URLs
    │           └── /compound/{phase-id}-{phase-slug}
    │                 └── unit cards (paginated)
    │                       └── /property/{unit-id} (unit detail)
    └── NO  → unit cards directly (paginated)
                  └── /property/{unit-id}
```
